<title>BELGIUM: EU SET TO BAN SOME DUTCH PIG EXPORTS.</title>
<headline>EU SET TO BAN SOME DUTCH PIG EXPORTS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's Standing Veterinary Committee, at a special meeting on Wednesday, backed a ban on exports of pigs from seven Dutch districts following an outbreak of swine fever, a Commission official said.</p>
<p>The ban, which will cover the districts of Nijmegen, Breda, Weert, Doetinchem, Rotterdam, Amsterdam and Apeldoorn, is expected to be formally imposed by the European Commission in the next few days.</p>
</text>
